Steps to Create an Ignore File for OWASP ZAP Warnings
Switch to the feature Branch:
Ensure you are on the feature/enabling-cicd branch.
   git checkout feature/enabling-cicd
Create the Ignore File:
At the root of the repository, create a new file named zap_ignore_rules using the VI editor:
   vi zap_ignore_rules
Add Warning IDs to the File:
Enter the following content in zap_ignore_rules with the actual warning IDs and your Kubernetes IP k8:30000:
100001  IGNORE  http://k8:30000
10020   IGNORE  http://k8:30000
10021   IGNORE  http://k8:30000
10037   IGNORE  http://k8:30000
10038   IGNORE  http://k8:30000
10063   IGNORE  http://k8:30000
10098   IGNORE  http://k8:30000
90003   IGNORE  http://k8:30000
Note: Use TABs between columns instead of spaces.
Edit the Jenkinsfile:

Open the Jenkinsfile and locate the docker command within the DAST - OWASP ZAP stage.
Add the -c zap_ignore_rules argument to the command to make use of the ignore file:
 docker run -v $(pwd):/zap/wrk/:rw ghcr.io/zaproxy/zaproxy zap-api-scan.py \
   -t k8:30000/api-docs/ \
   -f openapi \
   -r zap_report.html \
   -w zap_report.md \
   -J zap_json_report.json \
   -c zap_ignore_rules
Commit and Push the Changes:

Save the zap_ignore_rules file and commit your changes.
   git add zap_ignore_rules Jenkinsfile
   git commit -m "Add ignore rules for OWASP ZAP warnings"
   git push origin feature/enabling-cicd
Verify the Pipeline:
Trigger the Jenkins pipeline. It should complete successfully, with the warnings specified in zap_ignore_rules being ignored in the DAST - OWASP ZAP stage.
